.TH RCDU 1 "October 2026" "rcdu 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rcdu \- Linux disk usage browser with ncdu-compatible files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rcdu
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan directory entries and metadata, displaying allocated and apparent disk
usage. Directories include their own usage. Hardlinks count once in each
containing ancestor. File contents are not read, except cache marker files.
The selected directory defaults to the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-threads " N"
Scan workers: 1 by default, 0 automatic, maximum 255.
.TP
.B \-x
Stay on the selected filesystem.
.TP
.B \-e
Store extended owner, group, mode and modification time metadata.
.TP
.B \-L
Follow file symlinks. Directory symlinks are never traversed.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-rr
Disable deletion; repeated usage also disables shell launch.
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-1 ", " \-2
No, line, or full scanning UI. Exports default to no scanning UI.
.TP
.B \-q
Slow UI updates to two seconds.
.TP
.B \-f FILE
Import raw/Zstandard JSON or seekable EX1 binary. JSON stdin uses a dash.
.TP
.B \-o FILE
Export JSON; a dash selects stdout. One worker streams, multiple workers stage
observations in memory.
.TP
.B \-c
Compress JSON output with Zstandard.
.TP
.B \-O FILE
Export ncdu EX1 indexed binary, always Zstandard, with parallel block writers.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude PATTERN
Exclude matching components. Leading slash anchors to the filesystem root;
trailing slash matches directories only.
.TP
.B \-X FILE
Read byte patterns from a file.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude-caches ", " \-\-exclude-kernfs
Exclude valid CACHEDIR.TAG directories or child Linux kernel filesystem crossings.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore-config
Do not read configuration files.
.TP
.B \-\-quit-after-scan
Construct and finalize the complete memory model, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the full option summary. Detailed options are documented in docs/cli.md.
.SH KEYS
Arrows or hjkl navigate; Enter enters a directory; Backspace goes to parent.
q quits, ? shows help, i shows details, d deletes after default-No confirmation,
r refreshes the current directory, and b opens a shell.
n sorts names, s sizes, C item counts, M extended modification times.
a toggles apparent size, e hidden entries, t directory grouping, c counts,
m times, g graph/percent and u shared/unique usage.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Read /etc/ncdu.conf, then $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ncdu/config or
$HOME/.config/ncdu/config, then command-line overrides. Exclusions accumulate.
Each line contains an option and optional value separated by whitespace or
an equals sign. Blank lines and leading hash comments are ignored.
Prefix an option with @ to suppress its errors. This is not shell quoting.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
NCDU_SHELL, otherwise SHELL, selects the shell. NCDU_LEVEL is incremented
and capped at 9. Custom delete commands receive NCDU_DELETE_PATH and have a
quoted target argument appended.
.SH FILESYSTEM ACTIONS
Imports disable shell, deletion and refresh by default. Explicit options may
enable actions for JSON imports with safe absolute roots. Indexed files always
disable deletion, refresh and hardlink navigation.
Built-in deletion removes only scanned children and never follows directory
symlinks. Refresh failures retain prior observations. A scan is not a snapshot
of a concurrently changing filesystem.
.SH NOTES
Full UI uses /dev/tty independently of redirected stdin/stdout.
Legacy JSON preserves invalid UTF-8 filename bytes. A late enumeration error
after the first child cannot be appended to a streamed JSON directory object.
.SH AUTHORS
Aditya Gupta and contributors. ncdu by Yorhel; natural sorting by Martin Pool.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ncdu (1),
.BR du (1)
